  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1200 PM CDT Sat Oct 17 2026\n\nThe upper low will transition to an open wave trough as it struggles \nto move across the Desert Southwest before it becomes, at most, a \nsubtle shortwave late Monday into Tuesday. Upper ridging will build \nby mid week as another upper low moves southward just offshore of \nthe West Coast. Models are in fairly good agreement with the \nevolution of the upper low and upper ridge by late week. The upper \nlow is progged to move inland across the Desert Southwest before \ntransitioning to an open wave trough as it reaches the Four Corners. \nThis pattern would result in additional heavy rainfall for New \nMexico, but West Texas would be at risk of dryslotting as we move \ninto next weekend. Models do have some storms in the forecast, but \nthis will likely change as time moves closer. Ultimately, the \ndryslot risk will depend on the path of the upper low.",
